.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt SYSCTL.CONF 5
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm sysctl.conf
.Nd kernel variables set at boot
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
file lists kernel variables that
.Pa /etc/rc.d/sysctl
sets with
.Xr sysctl 8
early in boot, before any other service starts.
Each line has the form
.Pp
.Dl Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value
.Pp
as
.Xr sysctl 8
takes it on its command line.
A value may be enclosed in double or single quotes.
A
.Ql #
starts a comment that runs to the end of the line, and blank lines are
ignored.
.Pp
An unknown name, or a value that can't be set, is reported on the console;
the remaining lines are still applied.
Settings local to a machine may go in
.Pa /etc/sysctl.conf.local ,
applied after
.Nm .
.Pp
Tunables, which are fixed when the kernel starts, can't be set here; they go
on the kernel command line as
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/sysctl.conf.local -compact
.It Pa /etc/sysctl.conf
.It Pa /etc/sysctl.conf.local
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# The host name, until /etc/rc.conf's hostname sets it
kern.hostname=builder
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sysctl 3 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr rc 8 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
